# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values. NEVER commit `.env`.
# In Lovable, set these under Project Settings -> Environment Variables.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Supabase (frontend, safe to expose — protected by Row Level Security) ---
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT-REF.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EVERYTHING BELOW IS SERVER-SIDE ONLY. Do not put it in this file or any
# VITE_ variable — anything prefixed VITE_ is compiled into the JavaScript
# bundle and is readable by anyone who opens the page. Ad platform tokens can
# spend money; they belong in Supabase Edge Function secrets:
#
#   npx supabase secrets set META_ACCESS_TOKEN=...
#
# --- Meta (easiest — no App Review needed for your own ad accounts) ---
#   META_ACCESS_TOKEN     System User token from Business Manager
#   META_AD_ACCOUNT_ID    e.g. act_1234567890
#
# --- Google Ads (needs an approved developer token — see README) ---
#   GOOGLE_ADS_DEVELOPER_TOKEN
#   GOOGLE_ADS_CLIENT_ID
#   GOOGLE_ADS_CLIENT_SECRET
#   GOOGLE_ADS_REFRESH_TOKEN
#   GOOGLE_ADS_CUSTOMER_ID          the account being read, digits only
#   GOOGLE_ADS_LOGIN_CUSTOMER_ID    your manager (MCC) account, digits only
#
# --- Reddit (campaign endpoints are allow-listed — see README) ---
#   REDDIT_CLIENT_ID
#   REDDIT_CLIENT_SECRET
#   REDDIT_REFRESH_TOKEN
#   REDDIT_AD_ACCOUNT_ID
#
# --- Required by the sync functions to write results back ---
#   SUPABASE_URL                  auto-provided by Supabase
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY     auto-provided by Supabase
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
